⍝ ASCII names of glyphs: #name stands for the glyph
2 3#rho#iota6
+/#iota10
#rotate'ABC'
5#max3
1 2 3#in2
X#gets4
X
⍝ The longest known name is taken, so a digit or a name may follow
#iota5
#rhoX
#rho#rho2 3#rho0
⍝ Case does not matter
#IOTA3
⍝ Not inside strings or comments; #comment starts a comment
'#rho'
1+1 ⍝ #rho
1+1 #comment #rho
⍝ Functions can be typed in ASCII too
#del R#getsSQ Y
R#getsY#timesY
#del
SQ 4
⎕CR 'SQ'
⍝ ⎕ input is transliterated; ⍞ input is not
Z←⎕
#iota3
Z
Z←⍞
#rho
Z
⍝ ⍞ output continues the line until a new line is needed
⍞←'A' ⋄ ⍞←'B' ⋄ ⍞←'C'
'NEXT'
⍝ An unknown name is a syntax error
#nosuch
